        {
            "content": "The given angle measures $65\\degree$, and we need to relate the opposite side to the adjacent side.\n\nAngle | $55\\degree$ | $\\purpleD{65\\degree}$ | $75\\degree$\n:-: | :-: | :-: | :-:\n$\\dfrac{\\text{adjacent leg length}}{\\text{hypotenuse length}}$ | $0.57$ | $0.42$ | $0.26$\n$\\dfrac{\\text{opposite leg length}}{\\text{hypotenuse length}}$ | $0.82$ | $0.91$ | $0.97$\n$\\purpleD{\\dfrac{\\text{opposite leg length}}{\\text{adjacent leg length}}}$ | $1.43$ | $\\boxed{\\purpleD{2.14}}$ | $3.73$\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\purpleD{\\dfrac{\\text{opposite leg length}}{\\text{adjacent leg length}}} &\\approx \\purpleD{2.14}\\\\\\\\\n\\dfrac{GH}{HI} &\\approx \\purpleD{2.14}\\\\\\\\\n\\dfrac{GH}{3} &\\approx \\purpleD{2.14}\\\\\\\\\n\\cancel{3}\\cdot \\dfrac{GH}{\\cancel{3}} &\\approx 3\\cdot \\purpleD{2.14}\\\\\\\\\nGH &\\approx 6.4\n\\end{align}$",
            "widgets": {},
